From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 19:38:37 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 13/14] Keep the login code out of the debug log

The code entered to log in was written to the debug log as it was typed.
Whoever reads that log, or a log a user attaches to a bug report, could
use it while it is valid. It is now only said that a code was entered,
as is done for the password.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Submitted [https://github.com/UnitedMarsupials/tdlib-purple/pull/47]
---
 td-client.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/td-client.cpp b/td-client.cpp
index 5d443cc..dd52c88 100644
--- a/td-client.cpp
+++ b/td-client.cpp
@@ -782,7 +782,7 @@ void PurpleTdClient::requestAuthCode(const td::td_api::authenticationCodeInfo *c
 
 void PurpleTdClient::requestCodeEntered(PurpleTdClient *self, const gchar *code)
 {
-    purple_debug_misc(config::pluginId, "Authentication code entered: '%s'\n", code);
+    purple_debug_misc(config::pluginId, "Authentication code entered\n");
     auto checkCode = td::td_api::make_object<td::td_api::checkAuthenticationCode>();
     if (code)
         checkCode->code_ = code;
